    "contract": [
      "Directory listing, information, and reveal retain the requested entry identity and inspect a dangling symlink without requiring its target to exist.",
      "The literal symbolicLinkDestination is distinct from a resolved URL.",
      "resolve with noFollow inspects the final entry and reports notFollowed; resolve with follow requires successful realpath resolution. Intermediate components still follow filesystem path traversal.",
      "Resolution returns notFound, notDirectory, symbolicLinkLoop, permissionDenied, or ioError with an available POSIX error code. A failed resolution never supplies a resolvedURL.",
      "Input paths reach the filesystem without lexical removal of symlink/.. components.",
      "Default FileService implementations that do not supply resolution report resolutionUnavailable; pre-existing API calls retain their signatures.",
      "CLI parsing, Linux --project parsing, navigation history, browser snapshots, and supplied session-state paths preserve original symlink/.. meaning; session schema remains 1.",
      "Atomic session saves through a symlink/.. parent write to the filesystem-selected directory and preserve an unrelated decoy at the lexically collapsed path.",
      "Resolution, information, and reveal preserve the URL directory requirement. An explicit trailing slash rejects ordinary files and dangling links under both policies; a valid directory-link/ is inspected as its directory. URLs without that requirement keep link-entry metadata.",
      "URL.path and withUnsafeFileSystemRepresentation both drop trailing slashes on the observed Mac and Linux Foundation versions. A shared conversion preserves hasDirectoryPath without lexically normalizing the rest of the path. CLI tilde expansion also retains the original trailing-slash requirement."
    ],
    "deliberateDifferences": [
      "Absolute returns structured status and never exposes a partial realpath buffer as a successful resolvedURL. This is a deliberate API choice, not a claim to reproduce every readlink -f output byte.",
      "Absolute strict follow resolution reports a missing target rather than adopting stat -L fallback as successful target resolution. No-follow entry metadata remains available separately."
    ]
  },
